 \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"813c490be11e7f7c63b884d0ab5684381d8cfdf69404a1564558f652550ca0bf","event_uuid":"5474fd89-f9c8-4573-87fb-3a0617256468","position":{"commit_sha":"81ff6b91fec2d3fbdf3cf303597bdf28c76f670b","position":"1788243384629229001-5474fd89-f9c8-4573-87fb-3a0617256468"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c1098546b145b7b6efc7c9f674b094339610bdf4622995fca8e65ce04a51ab96","event_uuid":"0686f992-039f-46aa-ae07-bb458fef66dc","position":{"commit_sha":"1c3ebac5bb3edae436b83e9eac2c82c2a7eb4891","position":"1788243408812704001-0686f992-039f-46aa-ae07-bb458fef66dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"59bbf290edc0639856187bc7f022b7a7e5eb6439eb155fb8757919d5381ce9ec","event_uuid":"9ef4e9d6-61df-4144-b287-de32c681f1bd","position":{"commit_sha":"e333f8cbf19c0b1ac453e0787d7d67dbbc73fcd3","position":"1788243415094608001-9ef4e9d6-61df-4144-b287-de32c681f1bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d8215a4193cb60ce05d9902bc4afc19be232fca24a421be839e51051b7a698d3","event_uuid":"5f4ff89d-45ae-4989-8df3-df3bda96f5a9","position":{"commit_sha":"94cff4a6aeba6fd7a5ccb6ae868a8bac9ec9ad20","position":"1788244068062831001-5f4ff89d-45ae-4989-8df3-df3bda96f5a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5da7910a1163fbe8bb5ef725dad2e5347a77ea2db995c3728c53d278481083f8","event_uuid":"c1755c92-b854-4bf4-a98c-079ad06f6b16","position":{"commit_sha":"384ef341b7eb21a2ad2657e960a3ef8a32cd70a5","position":"1788244088506386001-c1755c92-b854-4bf4-a98c-079ad06f6b16"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fb38cb68748e7e5a582f32a941db06a4faabc33d70802daae07da0733987f6b8","event_uuid":"7cbc8682-481e-4943-93b7-3c7fe9c752b9","position":{"commit_sha":"384ef341b7eb21a2ad2657e960a3ef8a32cd70a5","position":"1788244090048714001-7cbc8682-481e-4943-93b7-3c7fe9c752b9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788046541848336939,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"279741eb-f000-433c-a59f-5e4c802ee2c7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa79-840b-da94-4a9e"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe current tickets branch stores ticket event dirs flat at `tickets/<id>`, making the root tree about 270 KB and causing every single-ticket commit to re-emit that large root tree. W2 changes only the on-disk layout to reduce per-commit tree churn. S1 history reclaim, W1 batching, and any live shared-store cutover are out of scope.\n\n## Scope\n\nImplement a fan-out layout `tickets/<sha256-2>/<id>` for canonical ticket ids. New code must read legacy flat and sharded stores during the expand phase, preserve all ids/aliases/events, and provide an idempotent ensure-registry migration. Do not run this migration against the live shared `.tickets-tracker`; fixture/throwaway stores only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] New ticket writes land at `tickets/<sha256-2>/<id>`; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout.py` proves a fixture single-ticket mutation makes the top-level tree bytes at least 80% smaller than an equivalent flat layout.\n- [ ] Alias, short-id, and full-id resolution are unchanged for flat, mixed, and migrated stores; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout_heldout.py` plus existing resolver selectors prove this.\n- [ ] Event replay/listing is unchanged for flat, mixed, and migrated stores; targeted reducer/list tests prove the same states are returned.\n- [ ] The migration maps every flat ticket dir to its deterministic shard, leaves no flat ticket dirs behind, preserves identities/event bytes, and a second run makes no commit; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout.py` proves this.\n- [ ] An interrupted migration working tree with some already-sharded dirs resumes safely on rerun without identity loss or duplicate commits; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout.py` proves this.\n- [ ] Migration collisions are fatal and atomic: two source paths mapping to the same sharded target abort before any partial commit/move; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout.py` proves this.\n- [ ] Merge-as-union reconvergence still preserves both sides on a two-clone sharded fixture; `tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout_heldout.py` proves both commits remain reachable.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Add `rebar._store.ticket_layout` as the single layout owner: sha256 first-2-hex shard/relpath derivation, existing-dir resolution, ticket-path-to-tracker-root reverse derivation, deterministic ticket iteration, shard-container recognition, pinned-tree path parsing, shard-container mkdir, and `migrate_flat_ticket_dirs_unit`.\n2. Writers create the shard container with `exist_ok=True` under the write lock before the atomic `os.rename(staging_dir, ticket_dir)`, preserving ticket+first-event atomic publication while an empty shard container remains benign; rollback/unpublish may leave an empty shard container, which fsck classifies as store data.\n3. Keep resolver outputs separator-free. `_ids.py` returns ids/names only; exact lookup and prefix/alias scans build the same sorted id index from flat and sharded dirs through the layout helper.\n4. Route all flat ticket path consumers through the helper. Required inventory: `_store/{staging,gitutil,store_usability,compat,ensures,env_identity,hlc}.py`; `reducer/{_api,_inbound}.py` (including `reduce_ticket` reverse derivation); `_ids.py`; `_engine_support/{field_reads,lookups,reads,validate,next_batch,commit_impact}.py`; graph `{_cache,_graph,_hierarchy,_links,_status,_unblock}.py`; _commands `{_seam,gates,doctor,composer,composer_edit,leaf,link_revert,unlink,claim,transition,transition_close,txn,delete,recent_creates,completion_candidate,compact,compact_plan,compact_rebuild,compact_recovery,compact_trigger,compact_txn,close_precheck,close_disposition,fsck_scan,fsck_repair,fsck_tracker_health,fsck_recover,fsck_authorship,fsck_restore,identity,session_log,tracker_maintenance,trusted_env_cmd,verify_authorship}.py`; sidecar/bot readers `{attest/authorship,attest/authorship_resolution,signing,metrics/{blame,event_metrics,sidecar_metrics,bug_trends},_snapshot/{ticket_view,ticket_objects},llm/{completion_sidecar,code_review/sidecar,overlap/queue,overlap/digest_sidecar,enrich_drain,plan_review/claimability,plan_review/relation_snapshot,plan_review/sidecar,epic_bug_screen,workflow/recorder},_io/{export_ndjson,import_ndjson},_engine/rebar_reconciler/{__main__,transition_replay,local_label_intent,impossible_links,inbound_translate,reconcile_check,apply_inbound_events,apply_inbound_records}}.py`.\n5. Register ensure id `ticket-layout-shards` in `_store.ensures`. It runs under the write lock, precomputes all moves before mutation, refuses target collisions as fatal/permanent, treats already-sharded dirs as no-ops on rerun, stages old+new paths, and commits once only when drift exists. If killed after renames but before commit, no partial commit exists; rerun completes the mixed working tree or an operator can reset it; targeted tests cover this resume path.\n6. Register required-capability token `sharded-ticket-layout` in `compat.KNOWN_CAPABILITIES` before any store stamps it. The migration appends that token so older v1.0+ binaries fail closed while current binaries read the store.\n7. Make fsck/store-health depth-aware at shared `foreign_store_path_list` / `_holds_events`, so valid two-hex shard containers are store data even when empty and unrelated top-level dirs remain `FOREIGN_STORE_PATH`.\n8. Update pinned snapshot readers to parse both `<id>/<event>` and `<shard>/<id>/<event>` through the layout helper.\n9. Document the durable layout scheme, sha256 shard derivation, migration, and compat-token semantics in `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/migrations.md`.\n10. Preserve expand-phase compatibility: before migration, readers handle both layouts and existing flat tickets may be updated in place; after migration, all tickets resolve to shards. Live cutover is deferred to the operator.\n11. The migration holds the write lock for local filesystem renames and one local git commit only; no network push happens inside the lock. The live 6,008-ticket cutover is operator-scheduled for a maintenance window.\n## Surface-Parity Census\n\n- CLI: in scope via subprocess create/comment/show fixture tests.\n- MCP/API: out of scope for live MCP because the server may run older code; accepted because tools delegate to the same library/core paths.\n- Library: in scope via `import rebar` create/show/reduce tests.\n- Automated callers: in scope through inventory updates and targeted unit selectors; no live Jira/LLM calls.\n- Dual-direction: in scope for local read/write and import/export; outbound Jira field semantics unchanged.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\nRun targeted RED/GREEN selectors: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout.py tests/unit/test_store_sharded_layout_heldout.py -q`, existing resolver/reducer selectors, and reconvergence/store path selectors. Final preflight: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test` with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on `PATH`.\n\n## Deployment / Rollback\n\nThis change ships mechanism only. Applying it to the live shared store is an operator decision and is not performed here. After an operator migrates a store, rollback is a tickets-branch revert or approved tracker-maintenance action that restores flat paths, relocates any post-migration sharded ticket dirs back to flat paths, and removes the capability stamp together; tests assert that post-migration tickets remain resolvable after the compensating rollback. No agent force/bypass.\n\n## Portability\n\nIn-process layout/migration only; no CI-provider dependency.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ticket_layout.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/staging.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_api.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_ids.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/field_reads.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/lookups.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout helper or prove sharded-layout behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"Route ticket-store id path composition/scanning through sharded layout 